{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"Exit code 1\n# Handoff and TODO\n\nSpun out of [POLICY_SPLIT.md](POLICY_SPLIT.md) and\n[LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md](LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING.md), 2026-08-13, revised\n2026-08-23. Items are\nsplit by whether the design is settled enough to hand to another agent.\n\n---\n\n## A. Handed off: cledger extension governance — DESIGN SETTLED\n\n**Repo:** `conversation-ledger`, branch `design/extension-governance`,\nspec at `docs/EXTENSION_GOVERNANCE.md`. **Depends on nothing here.**\n\nThe design questions this section originally listed as open are now decided;\nthe spec is the authority and this is only a pointer. What was settled:\n\n- **Producer identity stays out of `eventId`.** Two tools reading the same\n  source material *should* produce the same id — that is what makes capture\n  idempotent — so the writer must not be part of identity. The collision that\n  motivated the question is semantic, not id-level.\n- **A third-party kind is identified by `(producer.tool, kind)`**, never by\n  `kind` alone, with `producer.version` naming the vocabulary revision. An\n  earlier draft of this doc proposed namespacing the kind string itself\n  (`turnbridge/continuation`); that is discarded. cledger already carries the\n  producer as structured data, so it was redundant string-packing — and since\n  `kind` is in the identity subset, it would have changed event ids and forced\n  a migration across the nine repos carrying cledger notes.\n- **No migration, and no turnbridge change.** turnbridge already sets\n  `producer.tool`. The `renormalize` supersession pattern is documented in the\n  spec as the mechanism should a future vocabulary change ever need one.\n- **`ReadOptions` gains `tool`, `kind` widened to `string | string[]`, and\n  `linkRel`** — each backed by cited consumer code, with `actorId`,\n  `since`/`until`, and `producerVersion` deferred with reasons.\n- **Registration is the consumer-discovery form**: persisted\n  `{tool, kind, version, schema}` so a consumer can enumerate a ledger's\n  third-party vocabularies instead of hardcoding them. Unregistered kinds stay\n  storable; reads stay tolerant.\n- **The `ensureTransport` side effect gets documented loudly** — appending a\n  single event installs a pre-push hook and fetch refspec (`store.ts:172`).\n\n## B. Stays with us: still design-entangled\n\nNot ready for handoff — each is blocked on a decision in the companion docs.\n\n- **Per-turn origin rendering** (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING §3, §3a). Blocked on\n  the as-recorded vs. as-it-would-have-been call, and on adding\n  `source_event_ids` to the `continuation` payload first, without which the\n  walk cannot resolve a turn to its origin precisely (fabrication breaks\n  positional correspondence three ways).\n- **Marker reduction** (POLICY_SPLIT §4, and the six-marker inventory). The\n  one unambiguous win available now: opencode's `reasoning` parts are\n  plaintext, so `[visible thinking]` should not be injected on the opencode\n  path at all — it can carry a native reasoning part. Claude and Codex cannot\n  (unforgeable signature / ciphertext).\n- **Move human-facing disclosure out of the transcript into `plan.notes`**,\n  which already prints to the terminal and never enters model context. Applies\n  to model substitution, ancestor-unavailable, and size reporting. The import\n  notice is the one disclosure that genuinely belongs in context.\n- **Probe whether Claude's `system` / `attachment` line types reach model\n  context** (`docs/specs/claude-session-format.md:74`, `:196`). The two specs\n  disagree: claude-session-format calls attachments \"purely informational, not\n  needed for resume\"; cledger's `context_injection` describes them as material\n  inserted into the model's context. If they do reach context, the import\n  notice stops being a counterfeit user turn.\n- **Read `producer.model` / `producer.provider`** instead of `actor.id`\n  (LINEAGE_AND_COMPOUNDING §1). Independent of everything else, small, and\n  strictly better input for opencode's provider resolution, which currently\n  guesses by string-splitting the model id.\n\n---\n\n## C. TODO for Evin: Gemini and Qwen awareness\n\n**Not urgent. Live but untested as of cledger 0.21.0.**\n\ncledger 0.21.0 added `gemini-cli` and `qwen-code` capture adapters. turnbridge\nconsumes it via `file:../conversation-ledger`, so this is already in effect.\n\nWhat happens today, unverified:\n\n- Those conversations **appear in the picker**. `listConversations` has no\n  source filter — `conversations.ts:72` takes `producer.source` verbatim.\n- They render with a **raw source label**, since `cliLabel` falls through to\n  the bare string for unknown names (`types.ts:21`).\n- They can be **bridged out of** but never **into**: `buildPlan` native-resumes\n  only when `target.name === summary.source` (`resume.ts:109`), which can never\n  match, so they always fabricate. `parseCliName` also rejects them as target\n  arguments.\n\nSo bridging *out* of Gemini/Qwen may already work as a free feature — a source\nneeds no adapter, only a target does — but it is silently one-way and has never\nbeen exercised. Decide whether to (a) verify and document it as supported,\n(b) add real target adapters, or (c) filter unsupported sources out of the\npicker until one of those happens.\n\n(eval):1: ====LINEAGE not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UdopedwupqwcvKWEEyAgVo","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"324e5de5bd856853a4c994915cf2b93c8a3d6e6b","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","seq":48},"id":"ev1-a2b31b01b8325de5fc26da9a11aa90729d412fc4ff355b4f9cec00951fa7c697","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-24T02:19:04.150Z","producer":{