 subpath.\n- Extract to its own package when two things are true: the envelope has stopped moving, and there's a producer that isn't about conversations at all.\n\nWhy not split now: two `file:../` linked packages means every envelope change touches two repos and a version bump, and the self-capture tripwire (cledger records the building of cledger) now has two projects to watch. The module boundary gets you the API discipline and the peer-producer model without that tax, and it's a mechanical extraction later if the seam holds.\n\n## Questions that actually change the design\n\n1. **Does anything you're planning write non-conversation data?** context-graph's design says it's a derived, rebuildable view — read-only. Will intent-recall write annotations/recall events? If the only non-cledger writer is turnbridge writing conversation-adjacent edges, the generic store has one external customer, and that argues for the module boundary over a package.\n2. **Is `{id, seq}` grouping a storage primitive?** My lean: yes — call it something neutral (`stream`, `thread`, `group`) in the envelope, and cledger's `conversation` is what it means for conversations. Both cledger and turnbridge already need it. Do you agree, or do you want the store to be truly flat records + links?\n3. **Should `actor` leave the envelope?** It's conversation vocabulary but it's in the identity hash today, so moving it changes every event id — the migration the governance doc was trying to avoid. Options: keep it in the envelope as an optional field (no migration), or accept an `ev2-` id generation. I'd keep it optional and defer.\n4. **If/when it does become a package, which name stays?** `conversation-ledger`/`cledger` is clearly the app. The store needs a name, and that name ends up in every consumer's `package.json`.\n\nresult: Assessed the split idea — cledger's store layer (~3500 lines: notes, transport, re-anchor, redaction) is already content-agnostic in code; recommend making it an explicit module/subpath boundary now, with the envelope validated by the store and vocabularies validated by their producers (which dissolves the proposed registry), and only extracting to a separate package once a non-conversation producer exists; four design questions above.","type":"text"}],"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CeLqsYscSUt2WbyfQ7VYS","model":"claude-fable-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":83121,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":229,"iterations":[{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1124,"cache_read_input_tokens":83121,"input_tokens":229,"output_tokens":3342,"type":"message"}],"output_tokens":3342,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1081},"server_tool_use":{"web_fetch_requests":0,"web_search_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parentUuid":"39853977-a459-4a80-b15d-8f6162308f57","requestId":"req_011CeLqsVxVUAutWmLBwjryx","sessionId":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:13:55.619Z","type":"assistant","userType":"external","uuid":"5e54a087-3b39-45d8-91bd-936052b61cb0","version":"2.1.241"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-24T03:13:55.840Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
