{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"# Context Graph\n\nA typed, evidence-backed graph of how everything in a repository connects —\ncode, docs, conversations, commits — derived live from history that already\nexists (git and [Conversation Ledger](https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger)),\nnot stored as a second system of record.\n\nMost of what a repository knows lives in the connections between its\nartifacts: a file imports another, a conversation touches a file, a commit\nmodifies it, a bridged conversation continues an earlier one. Those\nrelationships exist in the underlying history but are never addressable as\nstructure. Context Graph derives them into one typed graph, every edge\ntraceable to the evidence that justifies it.\n\nContext Graph is deliberately a **data structure, not a product surface**. It\ndoes not commit to any one consumer or export format. Expected downstream\nconsumers — each a separate concern, possibly a separate repo — include:\n\n- **agent traversal tooling** — an LLM agent walking the graph to help a human\n  with a task (humans are not expected to navigate it directly);\n- **training pipelines** — future experiments and productionized versions of\n  [tagseq2tagseq](https://github.com/evintunador/tagseq2tagseq)-like models\n  that train by traversing text-attributed graphs, including e.g. a\n  `torch.utils.data.Dataset` wrapper;\n- possibly **[intent-recall](https://github.com/evintunador/intent-recall)**,\n  whose relationship to this tool (parallel consumer of the ledger vs.\n  dependent on this graph) is undecided.\n\nThis repository is intentionally at the design stage. Nothing here is locked\nin — it records current impressions and the shape of the problem, not a\ncommitted API. See [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the\n[WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n\n## Where it sits\n\n- **conversation-ledger** — neutral, immutable store of conversation events;\n  the firs